  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "antibody-llm-8039",
  "summary": "Biological ML work increasingly tests what models learn from data, from PPI shortcut biases to ESM-2 internal representations, rather than aggregate scores.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is scrutiny of what machine learning models actually learn from biological data rather than aggregate accuracy. An audit of protein-protein interaction datasets from HIPPIE, IntAct, STRING and PDB identifies shortcut biases tied to topology, self-interaction, taxonomy and function, and proposes an ILP-based mitigation. Mechanistic interpretability of ESM-2 finds reduced attention on disordered regions, yet embeddings and logits still recover radius of gyration and dynamic contact information. SeqMaestro and an oral-gut microbiome study apply interpretable models, the latter using SHAP site attribution to show complementary signals beyond accuracy. CryoConvNeXt and the glycan motif framework are more application-focused, recovering low-abundance cryo-EM species and raising true positives from 300 to 442 across 45 glycomics datasets. The interactome item infers negative pairs from experimental search space, addressing how training labels are constructed.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-09-15"
}
